  #:seon.task{:name "the-merge-gate-admits-new-lint-warnings"
              :plan "S5's merge (`48528db79`) published an unused `clojure.pprint` require and an unused private var, both clj-kondo warnings, onto HEAD (friction 6, `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-15/s5-remerge.md`). The gate's rule: `seon.cluster.source/lint-errors` refuses only clj-kondo errors in a file the merge publishes (the bar a lane commit holds). Proposal, for the owner to rule: the gate also refuses a warning that is new, meaning present on the merged file and absent in the same file on main, by diffing `lint-errors`'s analysis findings of both (clj-kondo's own finding keys, no hand list), so existing warnings (1768 on HEAD) never block. Done when a merge whose published file adds an `:unused-namespace` or `:unused-private-var` finding is refused with `:seon.source/lint-error` naming the finding, and a merge that only keeps existing warnings is not, proven by two deftests. If the owner rules errors only, close this task and record the ruling in the gate's docstring."}
  #:seon.task{:name "step-verdict-over-kept-chains-costs-gigabytes"
-             :plan "Lane merge-edited-tests (2026-10-16): `seon.context/step-verdict` over the 12 kept chain branches took 12 s and allocated 29 GB (about 1 s and 2.4 GB each), and one observer read took 944 ms and 2.2 GB. It runs after every eval request, so it is on the hot path. Profile with `seon.profile/measure` on one kept chain, name what the work is proportional to, and make it follow the branch's changes. Proof: a `seon.profile/measure` assertion on one step-verdict call, parent vs change."}
+             :plan "`seon.context/step-verdict` costs hundreds of megabytes whenever main has moved since the branch's last verdict, and an attempt's first verdict pays it always. Lane merge-edited-tests (2026-10-16): over the 12 kept chain branches 12 s and 29 GB. Live run 10: a cold first verdict 650 MB, warm 7 MB. Lane cold-verdict (2026-10-19, JVM mode on default's kept chain branches, `seon.profile/measure` per stage of `seon.context/judged-input`, thread allocation): `seon.cluster.source/publication` 250-610 MB (chain-79389614d0d3 609 MB for a delta of 3 identities, chain-806cdff35fd2 399 MB, chain-cd8a339333ef 254 MB); `seon.task/assigned-obligations` 92-149 MB cold (the `seon.cluster.registry/fork-point` walk, 139-152 MB: `commit-step` read each commit's whole stored record with its fused index roots, about 0.5 MB, where `datahike.api/commit-graph-record` holds the parents and branch in 34 KB, 21 ms and 6 MB for the same walk; patch `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-19/cold-verdict-registry.patch`); `seon.context/current-results` 106-131 MB cold, 4 MB with its runner kinds evicted but the branch value warm (so its cold cost is store reads, unattributed); `seon.cluster.source/merge-members` 27-94 MB; `change` 6-29 MB. The request's own allocation was about twice the summed thread allocation (1,340 MB against 650 MB): storage I/O on virtual threads, which `seon.profile/measure` does not count. Publication is the recurring cost: it is cached by main's commit id (`(db/commit-id main)`), and main moves between turns, so the same branch pays it again (chain-806cdff35fd2: 34 MB right after a verdict, 316 MB once main had moved). Its work is the reindex of each whole file the merge writes (`seon.cluster.source/proven-file` -> `file-rows` -> `seon.fn/analyze-entities` -> clj-kondo): 254 MB and 165 ms for `src/seon/error.clj` (3,078 lines), of which clj-kondo alone (`seon.fn.analyzer/analyze` on the text) is 163-210 MB and 90-115 ms; on a clean candidate `lint-errors` runs clj-kondo over the same text a second time. What the work must do: a verdict whose branch and the files it writes are unchanged since the last one does no file work, and one file proof per changed file text. Key the file proof by the content it reads (the candidate text and the analysis inputs `file-rows` reads), not by main's commit, and let the reindex and the lint share one analysis of one text; or decide with the owner whether the file refusal is derived only when every other clause of `seon.cluster.source/done-refusals` passes. Proof: a `seon.profile/measure` assertion on two `step-verdict` calls of one branch with an unrelated main commit between them, parent against change; and a row `:cold-first-verdict` in `seon.cost-estimate-test/estimates`. Read `seon.cluster.source/publication`, `seon.cluster.source/proven-file`, `seon.cluster.source/lint-errors` and `seon.context/judged-input`."}
  #:seon.task{:name "a-reaching-test-the-test-step-never-runs-keeps-done-waiting"
              :plan "b54d25f68 made `seon.cluster.source/done-refusals` require a current result from every reaching member (as the merge does). Risk: a reaching test the attempt's test step never runs (a declared-long test, or an isolated member deferred to the platform host) leaves the chain `:working` until something runs it. Check which tests the turn's test step skips, and make done and the step agree: the step runs or defers through the same path the merge uses, so a deferred member gets its result. Proof: a fixture chain whose only reaching test is declared long ends done once that test is green, without a hand act."}
